# Vendored LuaBridge3 (kunitoki fork) @ tag 3.0-rc12
- Source: https://github.com/kunitoki/LuaBridge3 (commit pinned by tag)
- Content: `Source/LuaBridge/` header tree (43 headers) + MIT LICENSE.txt.
  Tests, Benchmarks, Docs and build files intentionally omitted.
- Why this fork/tag: v3 reworked the library for exception-free builds
  (auto-detects _CPPUNWIND) and its CI tests Lua 5.4 with exceptions
  disabled — exactly this repo's Release configuration (xrCore.h bans /EH).
- Do NOT use amalgamate.py output: the amalgamated single header it
  generates at this tag is misordered and does not compile under MSVC.
  Use the multi-header tree with include root at `src/3rd party/LuaBridge3`
  (i.e. `#include "LuaBridge/LuaBridge.h"`).
- Verified 2026-10-10 with a spike (namespace/class/def/property,
  C++->Lua and LuaRef calls, pcall error path) against vendored PUC
  Lua 5.4.9, compiled with /EHsc- /std:c++17 /permissive-: builds clean,
  runs correct. Spike source (not committed):
  %LOCALAPPDATA%/Temp/opencode/lbs/spike.cpp
